  "notes": [
    "Static force integration: one evaluation of the surface tension acceleration field on an equilibrated (undeformed) circular droplet, then the traction is summed. No time integration is needed because the analytic target is a force balance.",
    "The dynamic counterpart (integrate until the EOS pressure inside the droplet reaches sigma/R) measures the same relation and would need of order 1/t_cap * 2 pi / dt steps, which is why the force balance form is the gate used in CI. See the docs for the equivalence.",
    "sigma_eff/sigma is the effective surface tension the model applies; a correct implementation gives 1 at every radius and every resolution."
  ]
